WEBVTT

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:06.190
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, amen.

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:13.470
The reading from the Sinaxadion for October 20th, on which we commemorate, our righteous

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:22.940
and God-bearing Father, Yerassimos, the new ascetic of Caffalonia, the memory of our holy

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:28.500
and God-bearing Father, Yerassimos, the new.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:33.100
Our holy Father, Yerassimos, came from the Peloponnese.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:39.140
In his youth, his devout parents put him to the study of sacred literature, in which he

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:42.540
showed outstanding ability.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:51.700
As a young man, he left home for the island of Sakinthos, and traveled thence all over Greece.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:01:00.180
From Thessaly, he made his way to the Black Sea, Constantinople, the Propontus and Calcedon.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:05.900
Everywhere he went, he sought out men who, being perfect in the ascetic life, could teach

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:12.020
him the art of arts and science of sciences.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:19.100
He arrived at last on Mount Athos, where he gathered nectar from all the flowers of the virtues

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:25.980
that he found flourishing among the many ascetics he visited, in order to produce within

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:31.700
himself the honey of purity of heart.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:38.140
He spent a good while on Athos, among the servants of the Mother of God.

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:44.260
He received the great angelic habit there, and was devoted to the practice of all the virtues

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:53.660
of the monastic life, perpetual fast, all-night vigils, tears, the elevation of the intellect,

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:59.460
tending to God in Isihia, and purity of heart.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:04.340
After some years, he went on pilgrimage to the holy places.

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:13.540
At Jerusalem, he was ordained subdeacon, deacon, and priest by the patriarch Yermanos I.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:19.820
In the years 1537 through 1579.

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:25.780
After one year serving at the Holy Sepulchre, he spent the following twelve in the service

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:31.420
of the patriarch, but never slackened in his ascetic struggle.

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:39.700
On one occasion he went into the Jordan desert and spent forty days in fasting and prayer

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:42.500
as the Savior did.

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:51.260
When he went back to serve the patriarch as before, eventually he left Jerusalem and continued

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:53.100
his pilgrimage.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:03:02.380
He lived for a time at Mount Sinai, then at Alexandria and traveled widely in Egypt.

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:10.900
After that he passed on to Antioch and Damascus, took ship to Crete and returned finally to

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:13.500
Zachimthos.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:21.240
He settled there in a remote cave where lacking bread and salt he lived on nothing but

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:23.980
a few vegetables.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:30.700
Despite his sequestered life, he was soon discovered by the faithful and many came to receive his blessing

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:34.640
and spiritual counsel.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:41.240
Saint Yerassimos was well aware of the saying of the Holy Fathers that nothing is as perilous

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:50.360
for a monk as the praise and esteem of men, and so he decided to look for another hiding place.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:58.880
He found a little cave on the island of Kephalonia where he stayed for about six years, but just

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:06.320
as a shining lamp cannot be hid, there also the virtue of the saint came to light and

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:12.320
the faithful did not leave him to converse alone with the one God.

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:18.280
Divine Providence led him to a place called Omala, somewhere on the island where there

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:23.240
was a little church and a miraculous icon.

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:31.640
Here God made him know for a certainty that the time had come to accept disciples.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:38.440
Five young women came asking him to take them under his spiritual direction and to transform

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:42.560
the little church into a monastery.

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:49.840
He saw therefore that he must give up the way of life he preferred above all other, for

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:57.600
the sake of sharing with his disciples the graces and spiritual experiences that he had received

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:01.040
in full measure from the Lord.

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:11.520
The monastery was called New Jerusalem and those who dwelt there seemed as angels in the flesh.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:18.240
Saint Yerassimus lived to be very old and was forewarned of the day of his death.

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:25.400
He gathered about him all his spiritual daughters, gave them his final counsels, blessed them, and

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:33.000
with joy and in great peace gave up his soul into the hands of his Lord and God.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:40.560
He died in the year 1579 on the feast of the Dormition of the Mother of God.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:48.840
His memory is kept on the 20th of October being the day of the translation of his relics.

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:58.120
Until the present day the body of Saint Yerassimus remains complete and incorrupt as if he were a sleep.

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:04.920
It distills a heavenly fragrance and works many miracles.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:13.360
The saint has become the patron of the island of Kephalonia and the protector of all the inhabitants

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:17.280
and their powerful intercessor before God.

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:26.800
Particularly notable is his power to deliver the possessed who are brought from all quarters in the presence of his relics.

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:40.200
The preservation of orthodoxy in Kephalonia in spite of many centuries of Italian occupation is due to the intercession of Saint Yerassimus.

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:48.840
Through the prayers of our holy fathers, O Lord, Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us and save us.
